{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "What Happened Last Night?"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Life in The Fast Lane"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 13}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange information about hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le13ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Unreal Past: Expressing Wishes and Regrets "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you talk about the unreal past, you use past tenses to talk about hypothetical situations. You use the <span class=\"strong\">Past Perfect </span>tense for unlikely or unreal situations in the past or to express wishes and regrets."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to talk about a situation in the present that you regret or would like to change, you use <span class=\"italic\">I wish</span> and the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span> tense.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I wish</span> we got along better.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "It means that we are not getting along, but it would be nice if we could get along better."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to talk about situations in the past that you regret, you weren't happy about or that you would have liked to change, you use <span class=\"strong\">I wish</span> and the <span class=\"strong\">Past Perfect</span> tense.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I wish</span> I <span class=\"strong\">had found </span> out about online dating a long time ago.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "It means I didn't know about online dating in the past, but it would have been better for me if I had known about it in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the following examples from the text. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sometimes<span class=\"strong\"> I wish I had </span> all the time in the world."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">I wish we could have gotten</span> together sooner."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">I wish I had done</span> something like this a long time ago. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">I wish I could</span> remember, but I forgot what I was going to say."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Colloquial Expressions about Time"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Colloquial expressions are idioms that you use frequently, especially in spoken English. There are many expressions that refer to time in English."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Colloquial expressions about time can refer to different aspects of time. You can use these to express different ideas related to time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here are some colloquial expressions:<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Lack of time:</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">pressed for time<br/> run out of time<br/> no time to lose</span><br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Have enough time:</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">all the time in the world<br/> take your time<br/> make good time<br/> free time</span><br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">The right time for something:</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">just in time<br/> in the nick of time<br/> high time<br/> no time like the present</span><br/>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you have any<span class=\"strong\"> free time</span>, you should come by and visit as well."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I know you're <span class=\"strong\">pressed for time</span>, so which days of the week are available for you?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "There is <span class=\"strong\">no time like the present</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "But Amy was able to <span class=\"strong\">find the time</span> and now she's a life coach."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sometimes I <span class=\"strong\">wish I had</span> all the time in the world."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I thought it was<span class=\"strong\"> high time </span>I got some life advice."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "find the time"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make time for"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Amy was able to find the time."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le13ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about time."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "no time like the present "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "used to suggest that something should be done now rather than later"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Never hesitate in doing something. There is no time like the present. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le13ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pressed for time"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "needing time; in a hurry"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I know you're pressed for time."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le13ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "free time"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "time that is free from duties or responsibilities"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: And Peter, if you have any free time you should come by and visit."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le13ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "high time"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a point in time at which something is considered to be due to happen; similar to \"it's about time\""}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I thought it was high time I got some life advice."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le13ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "all the time in the world"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an unlimited amount of time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sometimes I wish I had all the time in the world."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le13ob02aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, research six time idioms you think your classmates might not know."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Learn the definition, how it is used and have an example ready."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Split with your partner and join another group."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take turns teaching each other your time idioms."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take notes on each new idiom."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Vote on which idioms are the most useful."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find six time word idioms."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I learn the definitions and write examples related to the idiom."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present my idioms to my group members clearly and concisely."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I listen for gist and for detail."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give feedback on my favorite idiom."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le13ob02re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le13ob02re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le13ob02re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Amy and I know each other from a class we took a while back about life coaching.\nIt seems we've always been bird's of a feather.\nIf only I had 